            <ArticleTitle>Metal Quinolates as Phosphors for PC-LED Applications.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>967-972</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s10895-017-2031-4</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Metal quinolates, Liq Alq3 Znq2 Mgq2 exhibit efficient luminescence in blue green region and find applications as emission layer in OLEDs. In most of these quinolates the excitation spectra are broad in the range 350 to 410 nm, just short of emission spectra of efficient GaN based blue LEDs. In this paper we report metal quinolates synthesized by slightly modified method in which the excitation gets extended beyond 450 nm so that there is better overlap between emission spectra of blue LED and the excitation spectra. Therefore these phosphors may be used for PC-LED applications.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
